A demonstration of what Quickshell can do that a status bar cannot. One QML
codebase draws a floating bar, a live dashboard and a full-screen command
palette: the palette takes keyboard focus, searches the system's application
database as you type and launches from it; the dashboard's volume slider moves
the PipeWire sink rather than reporting it; the graphs are Canvas repainting
from /proc, the gauges animate arcs. The shell registers its own global hotkey
and exposes an IPC API, so anything can drive it. Restrained on purpose — the
capability is the point, not the decoration.
